Z||000007||Oreif||09-04-2001||12:30 PM||||For $300 Canadian it's a great deal. Just to get it to run with a new 2.8L would be less than $1000. With a 3.4L (easiest swap) your about $2000 or less. A 3800 supercharged is about $4000 and a V-8 Chevy can be done for $4000-$5000. The prices above are average estimates with you doing the work. You can find engines for less and save money in other area's. An 88 GT in stock form is worth $3000 to $5000 in fair running condition. So even if you sink in $1000 to get a running V-6, Your still below the retail value of the car.<BR>Note: above prices is in USD.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||14
Z||000008||FieroBUZZ||09-04-2001||02:10 PM||||If you have room to store it and work on it, then buy it.  88 parts are always valuable and just the body parts to convert to a GT are worth more than 300.00$<BR>Gary<BR>Bonne chance!||||reg||14
